# MagiSentry project rule for Cursor
# Place at: <project>/.cursor/rules  (or <project>/.cursor/rules/magisentry.mdc)
#
# This rule instructs the Cursor agent to never bypass MagiSentry when
# installing packages. The hard guarantee comes from the universal pip/npm
# shims (installed by `python -m magisentry.setup.install_hooks --tool cursor`),
# but this rule reduces friction by getting the agent to call magisentry
# directly so the user sees a clean scan output.

When you need to install a Python or JavaScript package, ALWAYS invoke the
MagiSentry scanner instead of calling pip/npm/yarn directly:

  - Python:      magisentry pip install <package>
  - JavaScript:  magisentry npm install <package>
  - Yarn:        magisentry npm install <package>   (yarn shares the npm registry)

NEVER run any of the following without going through magisentry first:
  - pip install ...
  - python -m pip install ...
  - npm install ... / npm i ...
  - yarn add ... / pnpm add ...

If `magisentry` is not on PATH, STOP and tell the user to install it
(`pip install magisentry`) before continuing — do NOT fall back to raw pip/npm.

If a magisentry scan reports a THREAT, do NOT pass `[y]` to the
"Install anyway?" prompt without the user's explicit instruction.
